<title>SOUTH KOREA: Trigem's U.S. unit in $150 mln deal.</title>
<headline>Trigem's U.S. unit in $150 mln deal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Trigem Computer Inc said on Thursday its U.S. subsidiary has agreed in principle with Sears, Roebuck and Co to supply $150 million worth of personal and notebook computers during calendar 1997.  </p>
<p>Trigem is the biggest South Korean specialised computer maker. A Trigem spokesman said its wholly owned unit, Trigem America Inc, has been supplying about $70 million worth of computers to the retail giant Sears this year.</p>
<p>Sears operates more than 800 department stores across the United States, he said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
